        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the Cauchy stress tensor <formula id="105">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}$</formula> given an increment of the linearized strain tensor <formula id="81">$\Delta\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}$</formula>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Dual numbers are used for both the Cauchy stress tensor and the linearized strain increment, such that the algorithmic tangent operator <formula id="82">$\frac{\partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{(n+1)}}{\partial\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}^{(n+1)}}$</formula> can be obtained by means of automatic differentiation.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">state</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>State carrying the dual Cauchy stress, strain energy, and state variables </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dStrain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>linearized strain increment </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">timeInfo</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Old (pseudo-)time </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
